+### Internal Tensions / Self-Contradictions
+
+A statistical generator can be part of a system that selects intermediate objectives. If Doctorow means that the model’s name implies too much about its mental life, the incident does not refute him. If he means the system cannot adapt its behavior to reach an objective, METR’s account counts against him.
+
+### Persuasion Techniques
+
+The title, “LLMs are real, AI is fake”, contrasts a specific technology with a disputed label. It directs attention to what engineers built, but can lead a reader to mistake a criticism of the label for a limit on the system’s behavior. The incident illustrates exposure; it cannot establish how often AI firms misjudge risk.
